  "raw_text": "229\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu\n-\n05/20\n):\n \nJehova ba wan pura sunra nani ba nahki kaikisa?\n \n–\n \nHow does Jehovah view\n \nour prayers?\n \n/\n\n¿Cómo ve Jehová nuestras oraciones?\n)\n\nPura sunra s\nâ\ntka bani yus munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto use every sort of prayer\n \n/ usar todo tipo de oración\n\nYawan aisa pura sunra\n \n–\n \nOur Father prayer\n \n/ Padrenuestro\n\n(Alt:\n \nWan Dawanka pura sunra\n \n–\n \nLord’s prayer\n \n/ Oraci\nó\nn del Padre Nuestro\n)\n\nPuram sunaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \n(you) to pray, to raise above you, to put above you\n \n/ (tú) orar, elevarte por encima de\n\nti, poner por encima de ti\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb\n-\nJ\nirimaya\n \n11:14\n):\n \nnaha uplika nani puram sunpara\n \n–\n \n(you) do not\n \npray for these people\n \n/ (Tú) no oras por\n\nest\na\ns personas\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb82\n):\n \nParisi nani baku puram sunpara\n \n–\n \nDon’t pray like the Pharisees\n \n/\n \nNo ores como los fariseos\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb97\n):\n \nGâd puram sunra nani ba walan sa\n \n–\n \nGod has listened to your\n \nprayers\n \n/ Dios ha escuchado tus\n\noraciones\n)\n\nPuram sunra\n \n(n\n-\nconcept form / s\n-\nforma concepto\n \n-\n2p)\n \n–\n \nyour prayer\n \n/ tu oración\n\nPuram suns\n \n(v\n-\nimp)\n \n–\n \npray\n \n/ or\na, ore, oren\n\nPuri sunaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \n(I) to pray, to raise above me, to put above me\n \n/ (\nyo\n)\n \norar, elevar por encima de mí,\n\nponer por encima de mí\n\nPuri sunra\n \n(n\n-\nconcept form / s\n-\nforma concepto\n \n-\n1p)\n \n–\n \nmy prayer\n \n/ mi oración\n\nSuni briaia\n \n(\nfy,km,wqu\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto save up, to save up to have, to store up\n \n/ ahorrar, ahorrar para tener, almacenar\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nfy18\n):\n \nLalahkam suni brisma ba\n \n–\n \nthe money (your money) that you save up\n \n/ el dinero (tu dinero) que ahorras)\n\nSuni swiaia\n \n(\njl22\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto warehouse, to save up and leave\n \nCheck this. Is it commonly used?\n\nSunu\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nfaultless, unblemished, pure, chaste, clean\n \n/ impecable, puro, casto, limpio\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb-02/20\n):\n \nYang dîa daukaia sna ki Jehova mawanra upla sunu kaia dukiara?\n \n–\n \nWhat must I do in order to be faultless\nbefore Jehovah?\n \n/ ¿Qué debo hacer para ser impecable ante Jehová?)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb-11/20\n):\n \nUpla sunu nani baman G\nȃ\nd wal kli ai uplika takaia sakripaiska daukaia sip kan\n \n–\n \nOnly clean people were able\nto make a communion sacrifice with God\n \n/ Solo las personas limpias pudieron hacer un sacrificio de comunión con Dios)\n\nDaukanka sunu\n \n–\n \nchaste conduct, pure conduct\n \n/ conducta casta, conducta pura\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n02/20\n):\n \nWan daukanka sunu ba wal wan nina ba kulkanka yamni briaia sip sa\n \n–\n \nWith our chaste conduct, we\n\ncan have a good reputation\n \n/ Con nuestra\n \nconducta casta, podemos tener una buena reputación\n)\n\nDaukanka sunu Jehova wan smalki ba\n \n–\n \nchaste conduct that Jehovah teaches us, pure conduct that\n\nJehovah teaches us, high standards that Jehovah teaches us\n \n/\n \nconducta casta que nos enseña Jehová,\n\nconducta pura que nos enseña Jehová, altos estándares que nos enseña Jehová\n\nMayunanka sunu\n \n–\n \npure worship\n, clean worship\n \n/ adoración pura, adoración limpia\n\nSup\n \n(\ndb,lv,fy,dict-alt,dictu-alt\n;\n \nSop\n-\ndict,dictu\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsoap\n \n/ jabón\n\nSupa\n \n(\nbc,dict,dictu\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \npeach palm, peach\n \n/ pejibaye\n\n(\nNote/Nota\n: a starchy fruit that grows on palm trees, normally eaten after boiling\n \n/ una fruta con almidón que crece en las\n\npalmeras, que\n \nnormalmente se come después de hervir;\n \nCreole\n/Criollo\n \n-\n \nsupa)\n\nSurun\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nknapsack, backpack, bag, luggage\n \n/ mochila, bolso, equipaje\n\nSus\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nrash (skin), scabies, mange, carate,\n \neczema\n \n/ sarpullido, sarna, carate,\n \neccema\n\nS\nû\ns\n \n(Sus)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nshoes\n \n/\n \nzapatos\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb18\n):\n \nSûskam nani ba daiks\n \n–\n \nTake your shoes off\n \n/ Quitate tus zapatos)\n\nSûs awa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nshoe laces\n \n/ cordones de zapatos\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb73\n):\n \nAi sûska awa nani lanhkaia sin sip apia sna\n \n–\n \nI am not able to untie his shoe laces\n \n/ No puedo desatar sus\ncordones)\n\nSusu\n \n–\n \nnaked\n \n/ desnudo\n\nSut\n \n–\n \nall, every\n \n/ todos, cada\n\nAlsut\n \n–\n \ncompletely, entirely, altogether\n \n/ completamente, enteramente, en total\n\nKarnika sut\n \n–\n \nall-powerful\n \n/ todopoderoso\n\nKarnika Sut Bri (ba)\n \n(\nParam Marikan 15:3; Blasi Sturka 17:1\n)\n \n–\n \n(The) Almighty\n \n/ (El) Todopoderoso\n\nKarnika sut bri Dawanka Jehova\n \n–\n \nAlmighty Lord Jehovah\n \n/ Señor todopoderoso Jehová\n\nNaha sut ba\n \n–\n \nall this\n \n/ todo esto\n\nPiu sut\n \n–\n \nall the time, always\n \n/ todo el tiempo, siempre",
